      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:8:65:12",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ جَبْرَئِيلُ ( عليه السلام ) يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ إِنَّا لَا نَدْخُلُ بَيْتاً فِيهِ صُورَةُ إِنْسَانٍ وَ لَا بَيْتاً يُبَالُ فِيهِ وَ لَا بَيْتاً فِيهِ كَلْبٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Humeyd Bin Ziyad, from Al Hassan Bin Muhammad Bin Sama’at, from someone else, from Aban Bin Usman, from Amro Bin Khalid, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Jibraeel<sup>as</sup> said: ‘O Rasool-Allah<sup>saww</sup>! We (Angels) neither enter a house wherein is a picture of a human, nor a house which has been urinated in, nor a house in which is a dog’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "12. Humayd ibn Ziyad has narrated from al-Hassan ibn Muhammad ibn Sama‘ah from more than one person from Aban ibn ‘Uthman from ‘Amr ibn Khalid who has said the following: “Abu Ja‘far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said that Jibril, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, once said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, we do not enter a house in which picture of human beings exists or a house in which people urinate or a house in which a dog exists.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
